    <item>
      <title>CNMC urged to refer airport baggage deal to EU under Article 22</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cnmc-urged-refer-airport-baggage-deal-eu-under-article-22</link>
      <description>Spain’s competition watchdog is “ill-equipped” to review the sale of Siemens Logistics to Toyota’s subsidiary Vanderlande without assistance from the European Commission, according to a request for an Article 22 referral by a third-party complainant.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cnmc-urged-refer-airport-baggage-deal-eu-under-article-22</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Mar 2026 17:35:09 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ireland consults on raising merger thresholds</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/ireland-consults-raising-merger-thresholds</link>
      <description>The possible raising of merger notification thresholds in Ireland would further increase the importance of the Competition and Consumer Protection Commission’s newly-deployed powers to “call in” below-threshold mergers, according to a senior agency official.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/ireland-consults-raising-merger-thresholds</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Mar 2026 18:17:17 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A clean slate: The Tipline for 23 March 2026</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/clean-slate-the-tipline-23-march-2026</link>
      <description>Former Assistant Attorney General Gail Slater is not disappearing from the competition landscape in Washington, DC. The conservative think tank American Compass revealed on Monday that it has hired Slater to chair its competition and technology section. Also in Tipline, Newsmax and several broadband advocacy groups have asked the US Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit to block the approval of Nexstar/Tegna.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/clean-slate-the-tipline-23-march-2026</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Mar 2026 20:39:05 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Judge questions adequacy of HPE settlement</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/judge-questions-adequacy-of-hpe-settlement</link>
      <description>The divestitures in the Department of Justice’s approval of Hewlett Packard Enterprise/Juniper Networks were so insignificant they may have been designed to “create the appearance” of a structural fix, Judge Casey Pitts has suggested, despite stopping short of rejecting the controversial settlement.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/judge-questions-adequacy-of-hpe-settlement</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Mar 2026 21:55:19 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Cloud interest groups urge CMA to “move quickly” in new SMS probe</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cloud-interest-groups-urge-cma-move-quickly-in-new-sms-probe</link>
      <description>Advocacy groups and stakeholders have welcomed the UK Competition and Markets Authority’s decision to probe Microsoft’s business software ecosystem, but warned the agency is reliant on Amazon and Microsoft’s “goodwill” to fulfil their promises in the country’s cloud sector.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cloud-interest-groups-urge-cma-move-quickly-in-new-sms-probe</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 17:11:53 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CMA targets Microsoft in fourth SMS probe, but Amazon dodges formal scrutiny</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cma-targets-microsoft-in-fourth-sms-probe-amazon-dodges-formal-scrutiny</link>
      <description>The UK’s antitrust watchdog will target Microsoft’s business software ecosystem in a new probe under the country’s digital markets regime, as the agency opted to accept voluntary action from Microsoft and Amazon to address concerns in the cloud sector.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/article/cma-targets-microsoft-in-fourth-sms-probe-amazon-dodges-formal-scrutiny</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 17:18:33 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>DOJ, HPE rebuke states for “careless disregard” of confidential info</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/doj-hpe-rebuke-states-careless-disregard-of-confidential-info</link>
      <description>States challenging the Hewlett Packard Enterprise/Juniper Networks settlement acted with “careless disregard” by publishing hundreds of highly confidential documents, the Department of Justice and HPE have argued.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/doj-hpe-rebuke-states-careless-disregard-of-confidential-info</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 18:20:25 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>What’s done is done: The Tipline for 31 March 2026</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/whats-done-done-the-tipline-31-march-2026</link>
      <description>Nexstar has told a California federal court that it is “impossible” to comply with parts of an order requiring it to pause integration with Tegna. The closing of the deal “triggered a series of actions that cannot be undone” and compliance could jeopardise the strength of the broadcasters, Nexstar argued in a filing on Tuesday. Also in Tipline, John Terzaken leaves Simpson Thacher &amp;amp; Bartlett and the Federal Trade Commission takes another swipe at the American Bar Association.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/whats-done-done-the-tipline-31-march-2026</guid>
      <enclosure url="/images/logos/gcr-logo.svg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Tue, 31 Mar 2026 20:17:03 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Meta loses bid to dismiss monopolisation suit</title>
      <link>https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/meta-loses-bid-dismiss-monopolisation-suit</link>
      <description>Photo-sharing app Phhhoto has plausibly alleged that Meta Platform used its monopoly power to suppress nascent competition for personal social networking services, a federal New York court has said.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalcompetitionreview.com/gcr-usa/article/meta-loses-bid-dismiss-monopolisation-suit</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://d2qu5xmcgmzxnb.cloudfront." length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
